<title>UK: UK Sept new car registrations -1.4 pct yr-on-yr.</title>
<headline>UK Sept new car registrations -1.4 pct yr-on-yr.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>New car registrations in the UK fell 1.4 percent in September compared with September 1995, the Society of Motor Manufacturers and Traders (SMMT) said on Friday.  </p>
<p>The total of new registrations in the month was 138,059.</p>
<p>Total registrations for the nine months to September was 1,657,234, four percent up on the same nine months in 1995.</p>
<p>The top selling car in September was the Ford Fiesta with sales of 9,257 followed by the Ford Escort with sales of 7,521.</p>
<p>-- Rosemary Bennett +44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
